illet into a 350 degree oven and cook until the pork chops and apples are tender.</span></p>","skin":"WRichTextNewSkin","isQaMode":false,"fullNameCompType":"wysiwyg.viewer.components.WRichText"},"comp-k1e0bhlq":{"translations":{"title":"Widget Didn’t Load","text1":"Check your internet and refresh this page.","text2":"If that doesn’t work, contact us."}},"comp-k1e0bhmp":{"html":"<h5 class=\"font_5 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-family:avenir-lt-w01_35-light1475496,sans-serif;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">To keep things light and fresh, I serve it with a green salad of mixed baby kale,&nbsp;spinach, baby chard and shredded romaine topped with my <span style=\"text-decoration:underline;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><a href=\"https://www.theglasspantry.com/post/2019/03/04/crunchy-salad-sprinkles\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">Crunchy Salad Sprinkles</a></span> then&nbsp;tossed with just a little&nbsp;honey mustard vinaigrette.</span></h5>\n\n<h5 class=\"font_5 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\">&nbsp;</h5>\n\n<h5 class=\"font_5 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-family:avenir-lt-w01_35-light1475496,sans-serif;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">Cheers!</span></h5>\n\n<h5 class=\"font_5 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-family:avenir-lt-w01_35-light1475496,sans-serif;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">~Melisa</span></h5>\n\n<h5 class=\"font_5 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-family:avenir-lt-w01_35-light1475496,sans-serif;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span class=\"wixGuard wixui-rich-text__text\">​</span></span></h5>","skin":"WRichTextNewSkin","isQaMode":false,"fullNameCompType":"wysiwyg.viewer.components.WRichText"},"comp-k1e0bhnn":{"translations":{"title":"Widget Didn’t Load","text1":"Check your internet and refresh this page.","text2":"If that doesn’t work, contact us."}},"comp